cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Practical Molecular Dynamics Course"
message: "If you use these materials, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hentabli
    given-names: Hamza
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9530-2815"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/practical-molecular-dynamics-course"
url: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/practical-molecular-dynamics-course"
abstract: >
  A hands-on, 12-notebook course that teaches molecular dynamics step by step, from Newton's
  equations and a hand-written velocity-Verlet integrator to force fields, thermostats and
  barostats, periodic boundaries and PME, protein preparation, solvation, equilibration and
  production, trajectory analysis, free energy landscapes, and protein-ligand MD of the EGFR
  kinase with erlotinib, using OpenMM, PDBFixer, MDTraj, MDAnalysis, and openmmforcefields.
  Every notebook runs in Google Colab with one click.
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - OpenMM
  - MDAnalysis
  - computational chemistry
  - drug discovery
  - free energy
  - education
  - tutorial
date-released: "2026-11-24"
